Here are answers you can give, organized by bullet. Each has the likely questions, a short answer in your own voice, and the follow-ups interviewers tend to ask. First, two claims to fix, because an interviewer may dig into exactly these.

Fix these two claims first

1. "…and expired tokens." This wasn't tested. Only missing, garbage, forged-signature and alg=none tokens were. Expiry is checked in the code (jwtVerify rejects expired tokens), but saying you tested it isn't true yet. Either change it to "forged and alg=none tokens", or actually test it: sign in with a test account, copy an ID token, wait an hour, and call the function.
2. "…rejects values not grounded in the source text." That's broader than what the code does. Only the deadline, link and email are checked against the source. Title and organization are just trimmed. Say: "rejects deadlines, links and emails that don't appear in the source text." Being precise here makes you look stronger, not weaker.

