Questions that test judgment

"Where would you not use GenAI?"

▎ "Anything that needs to be exact, instant or free: reminders, alarms, filters and counts, finding URLs and emails, auth, and deciding when to re-index. I used it only where language understanding is the hard part: reading messy circulars and answering questions in natural language."

"What would you change for production?"

▎ - "Gemini's paid tier: on the free tier, Google may use prompts to improve its products, which is fine for a demo but not for real users' CVs."
▎ - "Firebase App Check, so only the real app can call the function."
▎ - "An evaluation set before tuning anything else."
▎ - "Server-side index triggers instead of a client-side sync."
▎ - "Deleting a user's chunks when they delete their account."

"What was the hardest bug?"

▎ "A pgvector migration that worked in Supabase's SQL Editor but failed from the CLI with 'operator class vector_cosine_ops does not exist'. pgvector is installed in the extensions schema. The SQL Editor's search path includes that schema, and the CLI's connection doesn't. Qualifying it as extensions.vector_cosine_ops fixed it."
